# TASK 1 — Add Global Skip-to-Content Navigation

**Potential files:**

- `components/navbar.tsx`
- `app/layout.tsx`
- Main view/layout components, only where necessary
- `app/globals.css`

AGY identified that keyboard users must navigate through numerous header links and laboratory switcher buttons before reaching the main content.

## Required implementation

Add an accessible skip link:

**Skip to main content**

The link must:

- Appear before repeated header navigation in keyboard tab order.
- Be visually hidden until keyboard-focused.
- Become clearly visible when focused.
- Point to the current main content area.
- Work on the Landing Page, Directory, and all six laboratories.
- Remain functional when switching between `?view=...` routes.

Use an appropriate target such as:

`<main id="main-content">`

Avoid introducing duplicate IDs.

Ensure the skip link moves keyboard navigation to the main content, not merely changes the URL fragment without usable focus behavior.

Where necessary, make the target programmatically focusable using `tabIndex={-1}`.

Preserve existing navigation, sticky headers, and focus styles.

### Acceptance criteria

- First keyboard Tab reaches the skip link.
- Skip link becomes visibly identifiable.
- Enter moves focus to the main content.
- Works across all eight main views.
- No duplicate main-content IDs.
- Existing navbar remains functional.

